<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/26f3aea55637> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "garbage in, garbage out. Even the LLM says it's from a Reddit post." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5858" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/311c633334cc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Liz Reid, who was recently promoted to Google's head of search, wrote in a blog post on Thursday that the company had pared back A.I. Overviews in certain ways..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3701" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5ea916f8f8c9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The state of Nevada is currently in the process of launching a system, powered by Google's AI, that will recommend which applicants should get unemployment benefits after losing their jobs." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7100" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9bd81f7f3f6c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"should have rolled this out more slowly,\" said Patrick Hall, an assistant professor of decision sciences at the George Washington University School of Business." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3701" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c353a83c1700> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Listing image: Getty Images" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5858" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9d55ee4aeff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Melanie Mitchell, an AI researcher at the Santa Fe Institute in New Mexico, asked Google how many Muslims have been president of the United States..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5853" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f0d3fede0425> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sometimes, though, glancing at the source can save you some grief, such as when you see a response calling running with scissors \"cardio exercise that some say is effective\" (that came from a 2022 post from Little Old Lady Comedy)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5858" .

